  storyText: {fileID: 1934305302}
  fullText: "Why Roosters Have Combs on Their Heads\n\nOnce upon a time, there was
    a magician named Pablo who had a son called Juan. Pablo was a hard-working father,
    while his son Juan was lazy and disobedient.  \n\nJuan cared for nothing but
    fancy clothes and his own looks. Because of this, he refused to help his father.
    \n\nOne day, Pablo walked into his son\u2019s room to check on him. There stood
    Juan in front of a mirror, combing his hair.\n\nPablo was furious\u2014He snatched
    the comb from Juan\u2019s hand and, in an anger, struck the boy on his head. 
    \n\nThen he shouted: \u201CSince you love that comb so much, let it stay on your
    head forever!\u201D \n\n\u201CI would rather have no son at all than to see you
    remain a lazy, disobedient boy. I\u2019d rather see you turned into a Rooster.\u201D\n\nWith
    that, Pablo hit Juan so hard that the comb sank deep into his skull.\n\nBy Pablo\u2019s
    magic, Juan was instantly changed into a rooster, and the comb on his head became
    part of his flesh.\n\nSo the next time you see a rooster with a red comb atop
    its head, remember: it might just be the descendants of Juan. \n\n\u2013 THE
    END \u2013\n"
  previousRelic: {fileID: 1103283106}
  nextRelic: {fileID: 753920776}
